.TH CUBICLE 1 "2026-08-24" "cubicle 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cubicle \- link shared agent config and other files into git worktrees
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cubicle
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git
worktrees are ideal for running parallel agent sessions on one project,
but makes it difficult to manage untracked files across each worktree.
.B cubicle
allows you to have a single source-of-truth for files that should not be in the
main project repository but may need to be version controlled separately.
.B cubicle
keeps one copy of AI-agent configuration and any other files in a standalone
.I share/
repository beside a project's git worktrees and makes it visible inside every
worktree through relative symlinks. A managed
.B post-checkout
hook re-links automatically after checkouts and worktree creation, and
anchored
.I info/exclude
rules keep the links out of
.BR git\ status .
.PP
Projects are laid out as:
.PP
.nf
    project/
    +-- .bare/       bare repository (common git dir)
    +-- share/       the shared files repository
    +-- <branch>/    worktrees; each links to the top level of share/
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-q , \-\-quiet
Suppress non\-warning output.
.TP
.BR \-h , \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V , \-\-version
Print version and license information.
All three are global options, recognized only in front position, before the
command name.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B clone \fR[\fB--opencode\fR]\ [\fB--claude\fR]\ [\fB--repo\fR]\ \fIurl\fR\ [\fIdir\fR]
Create a bare clone of
.I url
to
.IR dir/.bare .
The first worktree is named after the default branch. Create
.I share/
and setup the post-checkout hooks.

The \fB--opencode\fR option creates \fIAGENTS.md\fR and \fI.opencode/\fR in
.I share
and \fB--claude\fR creates \fICLAUDE.md\fR and \fI.claude/settings.json\fR.
Without either option
.I share/
starts empty. \fB--repo\fR makes
.I share/
into a \fBgit\fR repository.
.TP
.B init \fR[\fB--opencode\fR]\ [\fB--claude\fR]\ [\fB--repo\fR]\ \fIurl\fR\ [\fIbranch\fR]
Functions as
.B clone
but create a local bare repository instead of a clone.
.I branch
defaults to
.B init.defaultBranch\fR,
else
.BR main .
.TP
.B worktree \fR[\fI<git worktree add options>\fR] \fIpath\fR
Run
.B git worktree add
with the given arguments, and update links in all worktrees.
All arguments are passed through to
.BR git .
.TP
.B link \fR[\fIdir\fR]
Update links to
.I share/
into worktree
.IR dir .
With no
.IR dir ,
update every worktree of the project.
.TP
.B check
Check the status of links and hooks.
.SH LINKING RULES
Top-level entries of
.I share/
(hidden files included except for
.I .git*
which are skipped) are symlinked into each worktree root. Existing correct links
and files remain. Links pointing elsewhere are left alone and reported.
.B check
additionally reports stale managed links whose config item was removed
from the config repository.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <common-git-dir>/hooks/post-checkout
The block required by
.B cubicle
is appended to the file and marked with
.I CUBICLE-MANAGED-HOOK-v1
to preserve existing hooks. Updates rewrite only that block.
.TP
.I <common-git-dir>/info/exclude
Ignore rules for the linked items.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on usage errors, setup issues, or issues reported by
.BR check .
Other non-zero codes may propagate from
.B git
when an underlying operation (for example
.BR clone )
fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-worktree (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jeremy Brubaker <jbrubake@orionarts.dev>
